        <headline>Coastal Flood Advisory issued September 26 at 3:18AM EDT until September 27 at 5:00PM EDT by NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Up to one half foot of inundation above ground level in
low lying areas due to tidal flooding.

* WHERE...Shoreline in St. Marys County.

* WHEN...Until 5 PM EDT Sunday, especially around the time of
high tide.

* IMPACTS...At 3.5 feet, water covers roads on Saint George
Island, is in yards, and is approaching structures. To the
east, inundation is occurring at multiple marinas off St.
Mary's River, Smith Creek, and Jutland Creek.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Tides one and a half to two feet above
normal. The next high tides at Point Lookout are 1:53 PM and
1:55 AM. The next high tides at Piney Point are 2:43 PM and 3:07
AM. The next high tides at Coltons Point are 3:19 PM and 3:43 AM.
</description>
        <instruction>If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be
closed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of
unknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone
property.</instruction>
